# Playwright E2E env. Copy to `.env.test` (gitignored) and fill in real values.
# Playwright auto-loads .env.test at startup — no `dotenv-cli` needed.
#
# ─── Required for the `authenticated` + `chromium` projects ──────────────────
#
# Persistent test user — used by auth.setup.ts to sign in once and reuse the
# session across specs. If the user doesn't exist yet, create it:
#   1. export SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=...    (from Supabase → Settings → API)
#   2. export EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project>.supabase.co
#   3. npm run e2e:create-test-user
PLAYWRIGHT_TEST_EMAIL=lifeos-e2e-test@example.com
PLAYWRIGHT_TEST_PASSWORD=LifeOS-E2E-Test-2026!
#
# ─── Required for specs that use ephemeralUser.ts ─────────────────────────────
# (auth-routing.spec.ts, onboarding-fresh.spec.ts — anything that creates a
# fresh Supabase user mid-test). Without these the ephemeralUser admin client
# throws on construction and the test fails before the first navigation.
#
# These are admin-grade secrets. .env.test is gitignored — keep it that way.
# The service-role key is the same one you used to create the persistent test
# user. Find both values in the Supabase dashboard → Settings → API.
#
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
#
# ─── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where to test against. Defaults to localhost:8081 if not set.
# SMOKE_BASE_URL=https://your-deploy.lifeos-6r5-eqa.pages.dev
